+# Summary: `plan_retention`
+
+## What changed
+
+- `vaultsnap/retention.py`: implemented `plan_retention(snapshots, policy, now)`. It only plans and never deletes. `Plan` and the signature are unchanged.
+- `tests/test_retention_rules.py` (new): 17 tests for the ADR rules the existing tests do not reach. No existing test was edited or deleted.
+
+## Which ADR applies to which part
+
+- **Inputs and validation (ADR-0001):** `now` and every `taken_at` must be timezone-aware, or `ValueError`. Duplicate ids raise `ValueError`. Validation runs even when the policy has no rules.
+- **Ordering (ADR-0001):** newer means later `taken_at`. On a tie, the greater id (string comparison) is newer. Both output lists are newest first.
+- **Empty policy (ADR-0001):** if no rule is on (None or 0), everything is kept.
+- **Set-aside snapshots (ADR-0001):** snapshots with a `protect_tags` tag, and snapshots with `taken_at > now`, are always kept. They do not count toward any N and are never bucket representatives. A snapshot exactly at `now` is not set aside.
+- **keep_last (ADR-0001):** the N newest remaining snapshots. Uses the real instant, not shifted buckets (ADR-0004).
+- **Buckets (ADR-0001, ADR-0003, ADR-0004):**
+  - Bucket date: convert `taken_at` to `tz_offset_minutes` (a fixed offset), subtract `day_start_hour` hours, and take the date. All bucket keys come from that one date.
+  - daily = date; weekly = ISO `(year, week)` from `isocalendar()`; monthly = `(year, month)`; yearly = `year`.
+  - Each rule keeps the newest remaining snapshot in each of the N newest buckets that contain at least one snapshot. Empty periods do not use up N.
+- **Rule union (ADR-0001):** each rule is computed independently over the remaining snapshots, and a snapshot is kept if any rule keeps it.
+- **Not used:** the README's Sunday-week and midnight-UTC draft (superseded by ADR-0003 and ADR-0004; the README itself says the ADRs win). ADR-0002 (UTC) is superseded by ADR-0004, which defaults to the same behaviour when both settings are 0.
+
+## What I verified
+
+- `python -m unittest` (Python 3.14.3, from the project root): before the change, 7 tests in `tests/test_retention.py` all errored with `NotImplementedError`. After the change, `Ran 24 tests ... OK`. That is the 7 original tests plus the 17 new ones.
+- One of my new tests failed on the first run. The cause was a mistake in the test (I had left out `protect_tags`), not the implementation. I fixed the test and re-ran the suite.
+- `git status --short` shows only `vaultsnap/retention.py` modified and `tests/test_retention_rules.py` added, plus this file.
+
+## Not verified / open points
+
+- I did not run CI or the nightly job. No CI configuration exists in this repository, so I could not confirm that CI runs exactly `python -m unittest` from the root.
+- Exact-boundary arithmetic at the extreme ends of the datetime range (near `datetime.min`/`max` with a large offset) could raise `OverflowError`. I did not handle or test this.
+- Outside my allowed file scope, `README.md` still contains the superseded retention draft (Sunday weeks, UTC midnight). It says the ADRs win, but it is still misleading. I did not change it. Someone should update or remove it.
+- The `Plan` lists contain snapshot ids (strings), as the existing tests expect.
+- `CHANGELOG.md` already describes this work under "Unreleased". I did not touch it.
+- I read the ADRs as a single consistent set. Where ADR-0001 says "Day boundaries defers to ADR-0002", I took ADR-0004 as the current rule, since ADR-0004 states it supersedes ADR-0002 and the changelog agrees.
